WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.077 --> 00:00:06.883
Jason sat in the farmyard playing a video game.

2
00:00:06.884 --> 00:00:10.112
Suddenly someone bumped into his arm.

3
00:00:10.113 --> 00:00:13.812
"Ugh!" Jason cried.

4
00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:17.165
"You just made me lose!"

5
00:00:17.166 --> 00:00:19.428
He turned to see a goat.

6
00:00:19.429 --> 00:00:26.091
Nina laughed. "The goat wants to play a video game too!"

7
00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:28.816
Chef came outside.

8
00:00:28.817 --> 00:00:32.887
"The peaches are ripe, so we'll make peach cookies today.

9
00:00:32.888 --> 00:00:34.803
Let's pick some first."

10
00:00:34.804 --> 00:00:40.174
The kids followed Chef to the peach trees.

11
00:00:40.175 --> 00:00:44.464
They began picking peaches and putting them in baskets.

12
00:00:44.465 --> 00:00:48.024
"I love peaches," Izzie said.

13
00:00:48.025 --> 00:00:53.844
"Me too." Jason climbed a ladder to reach the branches.

14
00:00:53.845 --> 00:00:57.624
With his hands full, he started to come down.

15
00:00:57.625 --> 00:01:00.582
But a goat was blocking him.

16
00:01:00.583 --> 00:01:03.402
"Move it!" Jason said.

17
00:01:03.403 --> 00:01:10.384
Bobby laughed. "Those goats are troublemakers!"

18
00:01:10.385 --> 00:01:12.736
Nina looked at the baskets.

19
00:01:12.737 --> 00:01:16.514
"Do we need all of these peaches for the cookies?"

20
00:01:16.515 --> 00:01:21.774
"No," Chef said. "But I'll sell some at my farmstand tomorrow."

21
00:01:21.775 --> 00:01:26.603
In the kitchen everyone read the cookie recipe.

22
00:01:26.604 --> 00:01:31.090
"Jason and Izzie, please peel and chop the peaches," Chef said.

23
00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:33.648
"Bobby, take care of the butter mixture.

24
00:01:33.649 --> 00:01:37.930
Nina, you can whisk the dry ingredients."

25
00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:40.883
Everyone got to work.

26
00:01:40.884 --> 00:01:46.125
Bobby mixed brown sugar and white sugar with butter.

27
00:01:46.126 --> 00:01:51.646
Then he added the egg, vanilla, and lemon juice.

28
00:01:51.647 --> 00:01:54.974
"Ready for the dry ingredients!"

29
00:01:54.975 --> 00:02:00.581
Nina was still whisking the flour, salt, and baking soda.

30
00:02:00.582 --> 00:02:04.519
She put in cinnamon and nutmeg.

31
00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:08.955
Then she added the mixture to Bobby's bowl.

32
00:02:08.956 --> 00:02:12.585
"Here come the peaches!"

33
00:02:12.586 --> 00:02:15.939
Jason stirred everything together.

34
00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:21.465
Chef lined a baking sheet with parchment paper and greased it.

35
00:02:21.466 --> 00:02:25.964
Izzie began dropping tablespoons of dough onto the baking sheet.

36
00:02:25.965 --> 00:02:30.251
"Keep them about five centimeters apart," Chef said.

37
00:02:30.252 --> 00:02:38.698
"Otherwise they'll clump together when they bake."

38
00:02:38.699 --> 00:02:42.520
Chef put the baking sheet in the oven.

39
00:02:42.521 --> 00:02:49.314
"Bake for 14 minutes at 175 degrees Celsius," Izzie said.

40
00:02:49.315 --> 00:02:53.274
"Hmm. We do have a lot of peaches," Chef said.

41
00:02:53.275 --> 00:02:56.799
"Let's make a few more batches."

42
00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:00.243
While the cookies baked, the kids washed the dishes.

43
00:03:00.244 --> 00:03:04.267
"We made a lot of cookies," Nina said.

44
00:03:04.268 --> 00:03:07.229
"You can take some home," Chef said.

45
00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:11.211
"We'll keep the rest here as snacks."

46
00:03:11.212 --> 00:03:14.536
The next day the kids were in the garden.

47
00:03:14.537 --> 00:03:18.185
They were picking vegetables to sell at the farmstand.

48
00:03:18.186 --> 00:03:22.665
"My family loved those peach cookies!" Bobby said.

49
00:03:22.666 --> 00:03:27.563
"I'm glad there are so many left over," Izzie said.

50
00:03:27.564 --> 00:03:31.111
Soon the baskets were full of vegetables.

51
00:03:31.112 --> 00:03:34.538
The kids carried the baskets back to the farmyard.

52
00:03:34.539 --> 00:03:39.265
Chef was bringing out the peaches.

53
00:03:39.266 --> 00:03:43.910
"A customer!" Izzie said, pointing to a car.

54
00:03:43.911 --> 00:03:50.279
"Oh no! We're not ready yet!" Chef looked around in a panic.

55
00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:53.799
"Kids, please grab the signs and the cashbox.

56
00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:55.817
They're inside."

57
00:03:55.818 --> 00:04:00.070
He jogged toward the farmstand.

58
00:04:00.071 --> 00:04:03.071
The kids carried the things to the stand.

59
00:04:03.072 --> 00:04:07.746
Then they went back to get the peaches and vegetables.

60
00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:11.294
"Uh-oh!" Nina shouted.

61
00:04:11.295 --> 00:04:16.451
Izzie gasped. "The goats made a mess.

62
00:04:16.452 --> 00:04:19.968
And they're eating everything!"

63
00:04:19.969 --> 00:04:24.785
"I knew they were troublemakers!" Bobby said.

64
00:04:24.786 --> 00:04:27.931
Chef groaned. "Now what?

65
00:04:27.932 --> 00:04:30.553
We don't have much to sell."

66
00:04:30.554 --> 00:04:32.868
Jason looked at the goats.

67
00:04:32.869 --> 00:04:40.415
"I have an idea, but we need a new sign!"

68
00:04:40.416 --> 00:04:44.505
Later the kids closed the farmstand.

69
00:04:44.506 --> 00:04:46.661
Chef turned to Jason.

70
00:04:46.662 --> 00:04:50.189
"Selling the leftover peach cookies was a great idea.

71
00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:54.431
Everyone loved feeding the goats too! Thank you, Jason."

72
00:04:54.432 --> 00:05:00.162
Jason gave a goat a cucumber. "Glad I could help!"

